From e0fc44524b9a141583d77ca9b4145bde432413f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild-Idler Patch Tool <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 21:44:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0231: Role-aware stat naming -- hero card gets
 Intellect/Agility/Strength, Crafting/Enchanting gets Main Stat

Only strength ever changes label; Endurance/Luck/Wisdom untouched
everywhere.

Hero card (HeroesPanel.tsx): uses HeroManager.activeRole(hero) to pick
between Strength (Melee), Intellect (Caster), Agility (Ranged) via new
roleAwareStatLabel() in util.ts. Also fixed a second issue in the same
block: this row was rendering the raw lowercase object key directly,
never going through any label lookup -- a visible casing change
(strength 15 -> Strength 15), flagged plainly.

Crafting/Enchanting deliberately does NOT resolve a real role, even
where technically possible (an enchant target's hero is only known
when equipped) -- avoids the same item reading 'Strength' unequipped
and 'Intellect' the moment it's equipped on a caster. Uses 'Main Stat'
uniformly instead, via new craftingStatLabel(), with a hover tooltip
(MAIN_STAT_TOOLTIP, one shared string). Applied to CraftingStation's
stat picker and its Enchanted display, plus both Enchanted displays in
EquipmentPanel.

describeStats() gained an optional useMainStatLabel param, default
false -- Replay Memories' loot preview (patch 0228, not part of this
flow) keeps its literal Strength unchanged.

No changes to HeroManager, stat math, or persisted state -- purely
display-layer.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit and npx vite build both pass clean against
the properly re-based tree. Confirmed no remaining raw STAT_LABEL[key]
reads in src/ui/ outside util.ts's own fallback. Ran the label-
resolution logic standalone for all three roles plus crafting context,
confirmed exact expected output before writing this up.
